# Scroll-progress site header

Part of the Madd Lines design system (`design-system.mdc`). Master brand and breakpoint rules live there.

## Architecture

```
base.css (tokens)
  → site-header.css (all header/nav surface styles)
  → SiteHeader.vue (template + composable wiring)
  → App.vue (<SiteHeader v-if="!isAdminRoute" ref="siteHeaderRef" />)
```

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `SiteHeader.vue` | Storefront header component; owns `headerRef` / `headerBarRef` |
| `useSiteHeaderScroll.js` | Passive scroll + rAF; writes `--nav-scroll` to DOM (no Vue re-renders) |
| `site-header.css` | Compact pill shell, constant see-through glass, three-link states |
| `MobileMenuDrawer.vue` | Unused while the three-item nav stays inline |

Admin routes use `AdminLayout.vue` — do not change storefront header for admin.

## `--nav-scroll` (0 → 1)

- `0` = page top (see-through glass pill)
- `1` = fully scrolled (same see-through glass, float offset only)

The pill stays lightly frosted and see-through at every scroll position — do not fade it to a solid fill.

```js
progress = clamp(scrollY / --nav-scroll-distance, 0, 1)
headerEl.style.setProperty('--nav-scroll', progress.toFixed(3))
```

Distance tokens: **120px** mobile (≤768px), **160px** desktop (≥769px) in `base.css`.

When `isScrollLocked()` (cart drawer): force `1` via JS. There is no hamburger / mobile menu for this three-item set.

## What scroll animates vs what stays fixed

**Animate with `--nav-scroll` only:**
- `top` float offset (`--nav-float-top`)
- (Vertical detach only — the pill moves down with the shell)

Glass, blur, and fill stay constant. Do not make the pill more opaque on scroll.

**Must stay constant at all scroll positions** (do not interpolate):
- Shell `width`: `max-content` capped by `calc(100% - 2 * var(--nav-inset-x))`
- Shell position: `left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%)`
- `border-radius`: always `var(--nav-pill-radius)` (999px)
- Bar height: `--site-header-bar-height-compact` (2.75rem)
- Three-link content (no brand mark in the header)

**Pitfall:** Interpolating shell width from full-bleed → hug-content shifts the links horizontally. The pill hugs `me` / `my art` / `say hi` at every scroll position; only surface treatment changes.

Do not put the brand mark back in the header. Do not bring back the hamburger for this set.

## Layout offset

`--site-header-height` on `<html>` is pinned to the **compact bar height** (measured once via `ResizeObserver`). Content padding does not change mid-scroll.

`html.has-fixed-site-header` enables `scroll-padding-top` in `mobile.css`.

## Breakpoints

- **768px / 769px** — header inset / type scale only (not a hamburger swap; not 640px)
- **640px** — product UI, cart icon, parallax (separate convention; see `design-system.mdc`)

## Gallery product overlay

`hideForGalleryProduct` prop → `.is-gallery-hidden` (`translateX(-50%) translateY(-110%)`). `body.gallery-product-open` disables transitions.

## Visual direction

- Compact centered capsule of the three links only — no brand wordmark
- Soft blush editorial palette — light constant frost, not SF Pro or heavy glassmorphism
- See-through glass pill at every scroll position; active link is an inner chip
- Link states: 0.2s opacity/background; respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (snap 0/1)

## Do not

- Reintroduce `useAutoHideSiteHeader` or hide-on-scroll-down
- Put header CSS back inline in `App.vue`
- Interpolate bar height, padding, or shell width with `--nav-scroll`
- Use `box-shadow: var(--focus-ring)` on header controls (global button focus rule)
